{
	chapter.17B87200B743A819.title: "1 - Age of Bronze"
	chapter.1CF1785C39EB5427.title: "Create"
	chapter.20C630433F1679C2.title: "Enchantments"
	chapter.3CB4E0817ACF82A3.title: "3 - Need For Power"
	chapter.5CD631EA34E20F48.title: "2 - Quest for Steel"
	chapter.7746B039D48B69B5.title: "Cook Up"
	chapter_group.2FC413AC43E10EA8.title: "Logistics"
	chapter_group.31DEF325C7771BCE.title: "Grand Questline"
	chapter_group.52D1DC8F77B1ABD4.title: "Get Buffed"
	quest.01A2BC12B4A64454.quest_desc: ["Now that you have access to both ethanol and plant oil, it’s highly recommended to combine them into biodiesel. This fuel is fully renewable and can superheat Blaze Burners. The only downside is that it doesn’t produce as many stress units as other fuels when used in the various diesel generators."]
	quest.01A2BC12B4A64454.title: "Biodiesel"
	quest.01A74E976017BAF4.quest_desc: ["Craft some more refractory blocks and combine them with a campfire to make a primitive smelter. This will be your first smelter to process ores into ingots. Sadly, this primitive smelter is only good enough to process a few types of ores. You will need a better setup for processing some of the ores you collect."]
	quest.01A74E976017BAF4.quest_subtitle: "It is like a furnace but primitive"
	quest.01A74E976017BAF4.title: "Primitive Smelter"
	quest.0365F0553B9FD1B4.quest_desc: [
		"The amount of food progress it takes to increase a stat depends on your highest stat value. This means that eating only one type of food and raising just one stat may cause problems later on, when you want to catch up on the stats that have fallen behind."
		""
		"Try eating a variety of foods to level up your stats most effectively. Also, in the beginning, your stats will be low, so eating complex foods that give a lot of food progress is a total waste."
	]
	quest.0365F0553B9FD1B4.quest_subtitle: "and how to raise them properly"
	quest.0365F0553B9FD1B4.title: "Your stats"
	quest.04D76DFCE0977520.quest_desc: ["Crush some obsidian, then turn the powdered obsidian into Sturdy Sheets by following the sequenced assembly recipe."]
	quest.04D76DFCE0977520.title: "Sturdy Sheet"
	quest.04F604F9C424A180.quest_desc: ["Shafts are used to transmit power. When shafts are connected, they form a Kinetic Network. The total Stress Capacity is shared across the entire network. This means the 'Stress Unit' reading is exactly the same at the generator as it is at the very end of the shaft line."]
	quest.05509EC0C743D5CF.quest_desc: ["If you put the tree tap on a pine tree, it will start collecting resin. Again, don't forget to put a cauldron under the tap. &4When the cauldron has some resin shown visually, you can right click on the cauldron with a glass bottle to collect the resin.&r"]
	quest.05509EC0C743D5CF.quest_subtitle: "It's sticky"
	quest.055A562C58D678B7.quest_desc: [
		"Nether can be dangerous. A big part of that danger comes from lava. Brewing some fire resistance potions completely negates that danger. Find some nether wart and magma creams and start making yourself bunch of these potions."
		""
		"They will be really useful especially in boss fights!"
	]
	quest.055A562C58D678B7.quest_subtitle: "Don't burn yourself"
	quest.05E6C17BE3A09418.quest_desc: [
		"In order to make a cast iron ingot you need to place an iron ingot with a coal or charcoal in a basin. Heat the blaze burner under and power up the mechanical press over the basin. You will have your cast iron."
		""
		"Cast iron ingots are heavily used in industrial applications. If you have plenty of it you can use them in also pipes and tanks. They look cool! "
	]
	quest.05E6C17BE3A09418.quest_subtitle: "Process the iron"
	quest.061D03EFDA18B795.quest_desc: ["Everything starts with flint. You can easily find flint by left-clicking on the random rocks you see on the ground. Try to get at least two of them for now."]
	quest.061D03EFDA18B795.quest_subtitle: "Because there is no such a thing as wooden axe"
	quest.061D03EFDA18B795.title: "Find the Weird Rock"
	quest.061E0C5D7AAFF9A4.quest_desc: ["Air Intakes are used to supply air to Blast Stoves. You will still need a pump to move the air from the Air Intake to the Blast Stove. Air Intakes can work as a single block or as 2x2 and 3x3 multiblocks."]
	quest.0844F17111764060.quest_desc: [
		"Even though there are more molds available, these four will be the important ones for now. With these, you can produce copper casings and bullet tips. Keep in mind that even though you can use some metal nuggets as bullet tips, it is always more economical to create tips yourself."
		""
		"The production of gun parts requires a small production line if you want to automate it, or you can just follow the steps in the workshop you have in your base."
	]
	quest.0844F17111764060.quest_subtitle: "Casings, bullet tips and more"
	quest.0844F17111764060.title: "Molds"
	quest.085221A6A34FAD2A.quest_desc: [
		"Well, what can I say? You did it. Take at least ten minutes of rest, please. Go outside and touch some grass."
		""
		"This is the end of chapter two. It was definitely harder than the first chapter, but now you have an amazing material to play with: STEEL."
	]
	quest.085221A6A34FAD2A.quest_subtitle: "It is a beauty"
	quest.08B52E5BF2A1FEC1.quest_desc: ["Molds are important for creating various ingredients, from ammo casings to gun parts. Create one and try to find a stone cutter or mechanical saw."]
	quest.09D775F6279BA7B7.quest_desc: ["Anthralite is mainly used in the production of gun related items. It's always good to have a good amount at hand, so try to mine it anytime you see an ore down there."]
	quest.09D775F6279BA7B7.quest_subtitle: "and its uses"
	quest.0A46B18AE68FE945.quest_desc: ["Copper armor grants great armor values. However, it demands many copper blocks, and most importantly, each armor piece makes you 10 percent slower. On the upside, it comes with great durability."]
	quest.0A46B18AE68FE945.quest_subtitle: "Feel like a turtle"
	quest.0A46B18AE68FE945.title: "Copper Armor"
	quest.0B4D6FCA7B65FDB3.quest_desc: ["Most basic diesel engine you can make, yet it is quite powerful. You pump the burnable fluids inside and it just generates large amount of stress units, easy and simple. "]
	quest.0CC8EE4AF22327F2.quest_desc: [
		"The Blast Stove is a multiblock structure whose only function is to produce hot air. It does this by burning a fuel (creosote or furnace gas) with air pumped in from the sides. However, to work correctly, it also needs two additional pumps: one on the side to pump out the carbon dioxide byproduct, and one on top to pump out the hot air. The hot air can then be stored in a tank or pumped directly into a Blast Furnace."
		""
		"The stove can work with a height of just two blocks, but I recommend building at least a 2x2 stove that is three blocks tall, so it produces enough hot air for the Blast Furnace to run properly."
		""
		"This machine might drive you crazy since there are many inputs and outputs, so be ready to tweak it as is needed. Make sure all the pumps are facing the right way, and that you get rid of the carbon dioxide fast enough."
	]
	quest.0CC8EE4AF22327F2.quest_subtitle: "Why my air is not getting hot?"
	quest.0CC8EE4AF22327F2.title: "Blast Stove"
	quest.0D954CD61A8505DC.quest_desc: ["The rolling mill is used to process ingots into rods, and plates into wires, in the most efficient way. You can also use rolling mills to make pasta from dough!"]
	quest.0D954CD61A8505DC.quest_subtitle: "It also rolls doughs!"
	quest.0D954CD61A8505DC.title: "Rolling Mill"
	quest.0E2EEF331FA2FB63.quest_desc: ["You can press any kind of seeds into plant oil using a Mechanical Press. If you don’t have access to any other fuel, plant oil makes a good starter fuel, since all it needs is some seeds and a press."]
	quest.0E2EEF331FA2FB63.title: "Plant Oil"
	quest.0F128DBC4BE56B9E.quest_desc: ["Well, if somehow you've lost the first two villagers, or you just have too many emeralds to spend, you can get another villager easily this way. This one is repeatable, but it's the most expensive."]
	quest.0F128DBC4BE56B9E.title: "Villager III"
	quest.0FD08E8432879BBE.quest_desc: [
		"The most important use of Brass Tunnels is creating splitters. In scenarios where multiple items are traveling on a single belt, you may want to split that belt into separate lines for each item. To do this, simply place Brass Tunnels side by side on parallel belts and set filters on output sides."
		""
		"Please check the Ponder scenes to learn more about this feature. Understanding it is critical if you want to build a fully automated production lines."
	]
	quest.109990FF08915350.quest_desc: ["A single diesel engine is reliable, but it will never be enough for a real factory. The Modular Diesel Engine fixes that: it can be stacked. Just place Modular Diesel Engines in a straight line along the same shaft, and they’ll join together into one big engine. They also share fuel, so you only need to pump it into one segment."]
	quest.11528C0E6C2CBB8A.quest_desc: [
		"The Gearbox relays rotational power in four horizontal directions. Its Vertical counterpart performs the same function, but for vertical connections."
		""
		"&2Note on Rotation:&r"
		"When receiving input, the Gearbox relays power to the remaining sides with reversed spin. In other words, if the input is Clockwise, the output on the other 3 sides will be Counter-Clockwise."
	]
	quest.1175B6B643A7330A.quest_desc: [
		"Brass is made from one part copper and one part zinc, mixed by a Mechanical Mixer in a basin with a Blaze Burner underneath. "
		""
		"Brass unlocks many recipes that help you build more advanced machines, and it is also used to produce ammo casings."
	]
	quest.117B81F9889C85D1.quest_desc: [
		"Fortune is probably the most important enchantment you can have on your pickaxe, especially in the early game, where every bit of ore matters."
		""
		"Later on, some key blocks will require specific mob drops. You can enchant your weapon with Looting to obtain these drops more easily."
	]
	quest.117B81F9889C85D1.quest_subtitle: "Be greedy"
	quest.117B81F9889C85D1.title: "Get more"
	quest.118BDC6E185E44AF.quest_desc: [
		"Welcome to Gundustry. Everything vanilla and modded has been overhauled to provide a meaningful progression system. Even though some of the systems are still similar, there are a lot of changes in the game, so please use this quest book as a guide."
		""
		"You can either follow the questbook exactly or just check the book whenever you feel stuck. Also, feel free to use JEI to see what crafting options you have."
		""
		"Please keep in mind that this pack is designed to be a hard, and grinding pack. If you have any criticism, suggestions, or feedback, please join the Discord and let me know. Thank you for your time playing the pack."
		""
		"[ { \"text\": \"Discord\", \"underlined\": true, \"clickEvent\": { \"action\": \"open_url\", \"value\": \"https://discord.gg/ndS7mSRPtR\" } } ]"
	]
	quest.118BDC6E185E44AF.title: "Welcome"
	quest.127CEBB2A9289887.quest_desc: ["Now you have access to anthralite, you can make relatively protective and very durable armor from it. Keep in mind that you can upgrade this armor to something stronger later on. "]
	quest.127CEBB2A9289887.title: "Antralite Armor"
	quest.143E64D2636FB050.quest_desc: [
		"Bauxite can be found in overworld from Y level 70 to -30. It comes with layers so if you spot a smooth basalt underground, there are probably bauxite close there."
		""
		"After collected, it should be crushed in the wheels to be turn into the dusts, so it can be used to craft aluminum ingots."
	]
	quest.14AEC5A182CA5CA5.quest_desc: [
		"Now you have cleaned hides, tree bark, and wooden cauldrons. Right-click on a wooden cauldron filled with water while holding tree bark, and this will turn the water into tannin water. Then wash your cleaned hides in this cauldron by right-clicking on it with a cleaned hide."
		""
		"Leather will be an important part of your progression, so make sure to get a steady supply of hides from your animal farms. Lastly, don't forget that you can automate this process later in the pack."
	]
	quest.14AEC5A182CA5CA5.quest_subtitle: "Is it tannin or tanning?"
	quest.14AEC5A182CA5CA5.title: "Make the Leather"
	quest.14D72D85465ECE97.quest_desc: [
		"Find a fortress in the Nether. Fortresses are easy to spot on your map. While holding an empty Blaze Burner, you can catch a blaze by right clicking it. "
		""
		"Some of the special recipes may require heating from a source. Whenever a block needs to be heated, place one of these burners underneath it and feed it with a fuel."
	]
	quest.14D72D85465ECE97.quest_subtitle: "Catch a blaze"
	quest.14DA94B03C10C44A.quest_desc: [
		"We briefly discussed changing speed using cogwheels, but remember the golden rule: Speed costs Stress."
		""
		"Example:"
		"A Large Water Wheel provides 512 su at 4 RPM and there is a machine consumes all 512 su at base speed (4 RPM), your network is at max capacity."
		""
		"If you gear that machine up to 8 RPM, its stress requirement doubles to 1024 su, breaking the system. To run at that speed, you would need to add a second Large Water Wheel added to your kinetic network."
	]
	quest.15E430478D321B91.quest_desc: [
		"The Mechanical Press lets you press ingots into sheets. It also has some unique uses and is required in some sequenced assembly recipes."
		""
		"With a basin placed underneath it, you can use it to compress items into blocks."
	]
	quest.15E430478D321B91.quest_subtitle: "No more smashing ingots"
	quest.17C1B725E15A650E.quest_desc: [
		"All of the burnable fluids have some unique properties based on how are they being utilized. Here is the brief explanation of all fluids you can utilize."
		""
		"Diesel: Top strength in normal and modular engines. Meant to be burn in engines."
		""
		"Heavy oil: Meant to be further distilled or used in huge engines. The weakest fuel when it is used in smaller engines, but the strongest of all in the huge engine. Keep in mind that utlizing them in huge engines makes the engine quite slow, so it’s built for raw stress capacity, not speed. "
		""
		"Gasoline: Makes engines work faster with good strength. Best used when machines need speed rather than raw stress capacity."
		""
		"LPG: fast and the best heater. Spins the engines as fast as gasoline but with less strength. Blaze burners love to consume LPG, can be used as an alternative to blaze cake when used in  blaze burners with straw."
		""
		"Kerosene: General all rounder. Nearly diesel level power with same level of speed."
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		""
		"Biodiesel: the renewable diesel replacement. Not strong as diesel but has same power as gasoline at normal speed. Its strength is that players can make it from farming instead of oil."
		""
		"Ethanol: renewable and slightly fast. Weak, but runs a little faster than diesel. Also renewable from crops."
		""
		"Plant oil: the starter fuel. Weak, and slow. Mainly useful before a player has any oil processing."
	]
	quest.17C1B725E15A650E.quest_subtitle: "Info about the fluids"
	quest.17C1B725E15A650E.title: "Fuel and You"
	quest.180DB0034CCAFE86.title: "Shotguns"
	quest.18252BE5D32FA3C7.quest_desc: ["Ethanol is made in a Fermenter by fermenting crops with bone meal. It works as a fuel on its own, but it’s best to process it further."]
	quest.18252BE5D32FA3C7.title: "Ethanol"
	quest.1850E79EF3856462.quest_desc: ["Mine an obsidian block to make your portal to Nether. "]
	quest.1850E79EF3856462.quest_subtitle: "It takes 10 blocks to make a portal"
	quest.18A268FBFE9A24E7.quest_desc: ["Heat ethylene or propylene in the mixer multiblock to get molten plastic, then use Casting Basins to cast it into ingots. You’ll need a lot of these, so make them in bulk whenever you need more."]
	quest.1922A29F151CA9E6.quest_desc: ["If you have a connected set of Encased Chain Drives and want to modify the RPM of a specific one, you can replace it with this block. It allows you to adjust the speed based on a Redstone signal. For more details, please check the 'Ponder' scenes."]
	quest.195F0D9A1462934E.quest_desc: ["The Oil Scanner is a simple handheld device that checks whether a chunk has oil. Just right click with it and you’ll see how it works. A quick note from my own tests: even a little oil is still a LOT of oil, unless you’ve gone completely insane with this factory business. So don’t get obsessed with finding the biggest deposit. That said, I might have heard somewhere that desert biomes have better oil deposits, but I’m not sure."]
	quest.195F0D9A1462934E.quest_subtitle: "Find the oil"
	quest.195F16FEB903088C.quest_desc: [
		"Well, you were probably expecting something more complicated than putting sand in a smelter, but here we are... "
		""
		"Just put some sand in the primitive smelter and craft glass. Then you can craft bottles from these glasses in a crafting table."
	]
	quest.195F16FEB903088C.quest_subtitle: "Melt some sand"
	quest.1B46AB0B04FF5C45.quest_desc: [
		"Basins are primarily used for Mixing recipes, but they also support Compacting, Pressurizing, and Casting, depending on what machine you place above them. This is also your only way to press ingots into blocks so far."
		""
		"Take your time to check the recipes in JEI to get an idea of the possibilities. Also, don't forget to check the 'Ponder' scene for the Basin to understand the basics."
	]
	quest.1CA74D575C8D3DD6.quest_desc: ["You can craft a primitive version of a cauldron and use it for leatherworking. If you fill the cauldron with water and then right-click it while holding tree bark, you will notice that the water will turn into tannin fluid. Don't forget that wooden cauldron can only hold water or tannin fluid."]
	quest.1CA74D575C8D3DD6.quest_subtitle: "Made of wood"
	quest.1CA74D575C8D3DD6.title: "Wooden Cauldron"
	quest.1D1C4B00194D3F96.quest_desc: ["Molds are a one use, primitive way to produce tool parts early on. They go in the utility smelter along with the metal block to form tool parts. Please note that only certain metal blocks can be turned into tool parts this way."]
	quest.1D1C4B00194D3F96.quest_subtitle: "Cheap molds"
	quest.1D1C4B00194D3F96.title: "Molds"
	quest.1EA49778E91121DB.quest_desc: ["The bloomery is an expensive smelter that allows you to process iron and anthralite ores. It also processes ores faster than the primitive smelter does."]
	quest.1EA49778E91121DB.quest_subtitle: "Ok, bloomer"
	quest.1F4482A99A6A6F13.quest_desc: ["Mix steel, nickel and silicon together to create magnetic alloy. It’s used in electrical crafting recipes, but for most importantly for making magnets."]
	quest.1FC17EA7FFC6C568.quest_desc: ["Well, I hope you managed to hunt down some skeletons last night, because we need some bones. Turn the bones  into bonemeal and add clay, gravel, and sand to the mix to create refractory clay. This clay can then be turned into a brick on a campfire. Finally, simply combine 4 refractory bricks to create a refractory block."]
	quest.1FC17EA7FFC6C568.quest_subtitle: "For special furnace"
	quest.1FC17EA7FFC6C568.title: "Special Bricks"
	quest.1FF9C3F9882728C3.quest_desc: [
		"You can get naphtha either by refining crude oil in a 6-step distillation tower, or by refining heavy oil in a 5-step distillation tower."
		""
		"This fluid can’t be used as fuel, but it has a very important use: process it in the mixer multiblock to make plastic."
	]
	quest.1FF9C3F9882728C3.title: "Naphtha"
	quest.205794BD8120D5E8.quest_desc: [
		"Fluid transportation is quite simple: fluids flow in the direction the pump is facing. You can see this direction as arrows on the Mechanical Pump block. To change the direction, right click the pump with a Create Wrench."
		""
		"You can store fluids in a Fluid Tank. Tanks can be stacked on top of each other to create bigger tanks."
		""
		"Spouts placed on top of Depots can be used to create various items that require fluids. You will also need a Spout to fill buckets. To empty a filled bucket back into your system, simply right click an Item Drain with it."
	]
	quest.205794BD8120D5E8.title: "Fluid Transportation"
	quest.2197F47D47543A57.quest_desc: [
		"If you take a brass ingot and enhance it with redstone dust, blaze powder and some quartz, you will get a treated brass blend. Then, using a Bloomery, you can turn this blend into treated brass ingots."
		""
		"This enhanced version of brass will be used to craft certain guns and power armor parts, but for now, its only use is to create treated brass armor."
	]
	quest.2197F47D47543A57.title: "Treated Brass"
	quest.21BDE61EA5A3867B.quest_desc: [
		"Some multiblocks, such as the Arc Furnace, need more current to work. Since Graphite Electrodes have a resistance of 300 ohms, we need to raise our voltage to at least 1.5 kV to get a working Arc Furnace. Small generators can only produce up to 255 V, which means we need to set up a 6-step-up Large Transformer. Here’s how to do it, step by step:"
		""
		"Make two Large Coils, one with 100 turns and one with 600 turns. For the 600 turn coil, set your Winding Machine to 60 and put a Large Coil back into the machine."
		""
		"First, place the 100 turn Large Coil Block on the input side, then place the 600 turn Large Coil Block next to it."
		""
		"&2Now the important part:&r while holding a Laminated Magnetic Alloy Block, first right click the 100 turn Large Coil. If you click the 600 turn one first, the transformer will become a 0.17 step instead of a 6-step."
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Then, right click either coil with a steel block, followed by a bucket of lubricant. Check the blocks with the Multimeter and make sure it says 6. Now you just need to connect the cables."
		""
		"With 4 generators running at 256 RPM and this 6-step transformer, you can power an Arc Furnace. If your generators run slower, they’ll produce less than 255 V, so you might need a transformer with more steps."
	]
	quest.21BDE61EA5A3867B.quest_subtitle: "And not get crazy in the process"
	quest.21BDE61EA5A3867B.title: "How to Setup a Transformer"
	quest.222672CA2A6CEBDE.quest_desc: [
		"Iron produced by the bloomery first comes out as iron blooms. These blooms contain impurities that need to be removed. Use your hammer to clean these impurities from the bloom. "
		""
		"Later on, you can automate this step using a mechanical press. Keep an eye on it while doing that, because as soon as the last bloom is pressed into an ingot, they will start being processed into iron plates."
	]
	quest.222672CA2A6CEBDE.quest_subtitle: "Beat your bloom"
	quest.222672CA2A6CEBDE.title: "How to Make Iron"
	quest.223E0F90DF7BC8EF.quest_desc: [
		"Shafts are good for straight lines, but Cogwheels allow you to transmit power laterally."
		""
		"They also function as a gearbox. By connecting a Large Cogwheel to a Small Cogwheel, you can change the rotation speed:"
		""
		"Speed Up: Large turning Small = 2x Speed."
		""
		"Slow Down: Small turning Large = ½ Speed."
		""
		"You can chain these together to create a shifting system for your network."
	]
	quest.2294A47E5FF5EC56.quest_desc: ["Just a few tips in case you choose the violent option. The raid boss, the Federal Warlord, will be summoned along with some zombies carrying guns. If you’re out in the open, you’ll get blasted with serious firepower. If you haven’t already, consider getting some armor with Projectile Protection enchantments."]
	quest.23F309DEFD75AB7D.quest_desc: ["The Steel Mechanism is the tier 3 component for your factory. It’s used in some of the key industrial blocks you’ll need to progress through the pack. Set up a new production line just for Steel Mechanisms, since it will be required for further components in the future."]
	quest.2522ECDBA2481D98.quest_desc: [
		"When you place a Steel Distillation Controller on a Steel Fluid Tank, you’ll see the block change shape. Check the Ponder scenes to set up your refinery correctly. You’ll also see a gauge on the side of the tank. It shows how fast your distillation will be, so you might want to build a 2x2 or even a 3x3 tank to speed up the process."
		""
		"The recipes for oil and oil products change with the height of your refinery. Check JEI to see which recipe is most useful to you. Keep in mind that more byproducts isn’t always better, because you’ll have to deal with any excess you have no use for. However, distillation output blocks have an option to void excess byproducts. You can find it by right clicking any distillation output block."
	]
	quest.25420C3151C8E1F7.quest_desc: ["&4Take one flint in your main hand and another in your off hand, then start knapping by right-clicking.&r Keep hitting until you get yourself a flint axe head, then simply combine it with a stick in your crafting grid to get an axe. If you have a hard time finding sticks, remember that you can craft a stick with a sapling now."]
	quest.25420C3151C8E1F7.quest_subtitle: "Then put it on a stick"
	quest.25420C3151C8E1F7.title: "Knap It"
	quest.267CC91AF2F99C60.quest_desc: [
		"Place some stripped logs on the floor. Then, equip some Andesite Alloys and right click on the stripped logs. The logs will turn into Andesite Casings."
		""
		"These casings will be used in lot of blocks. Don't be shy to craft a lot of them. Use a wrench to collect them instantly."
		""
		"You can also use them decoratively to hide shafts and this doesn't consume the casing."
	]
	quest.27F1926054B3E2EF.quest_desc: ["Tunnels are one of the most important blocks when it comes to belt logistics. However, there isn’t much you can do with Andesite Tunnels other than splitting a single item from a stack moving along a belt. So better start crafting Brass Tunnels instead."]
	quest.281F8D258F5C6118.quest_desc: [
		"Now that you have a rolling mill, you can turn some spare iron plates into wires. These wires can then be crafted into barbed wire. "
		""
		"When placed strategically, it can buy you some time while you shoot at the rushing enemies."
	]
	quest.281F8D258F5C6118.title: "DIY Home Defense"
	quest.28C99197C75DEAAB.quest_desc: ["Clutches act as an on/off switch for your Kinetic Network. If you don't want certain machines to consume your precious Kinetic Stress, place a Clutch to turn them on and off whenever you need."]
	quest.28F7DD2AD0DBA96E.quest_desc: ["Now that you have an Arc Furnace, you don’t need to collect black steel from the Frosted Prison mobs anymore. Just put steel ingots and vanadium nuggets into the Arc Furnace (the recipe is shown under chemical vat in JEI), and they’ll turn into black steel ingots."]
	quest.2A8A734DE2CFB1D5.quest_desc: ["Adding vanadium makes steel slightly stronger. With black steel, you can craft tools that are more durable and sharper than steel ones."]
	quest.2A8A734DE2CFB1D5.title: "Black Steel Tools"
	quest.2AA89B5D94077E49.quest_desc: ["This is your first primitive ammunition. Considering how ineffective your tools are at killing mobs, you'd better craft some of these and keep shooting at them."]
	quest.2AA89B5D94077E49.quest_subtitle: "So anyway I started blasting"
	quest.2AA89B5D94077E49.title: "Powder Balls"
	quest.2BE35E278D29FE7F.quest_desc: ["The Polarizer has only one function, but it’s an important one: it turns magnetic alloy into magnets without any loss, unlike the old “catch the lightning” method."]
	quest.2CE689A15AB82111.quest_desc: ["You can make Brass Casings by right clicking a stripped log with a brass ingot. These blocks are used in more advanced Create machines that will make your life easier."]
	quest.2CE689A15AB82111.quest_subtitle: "Shiny casings"
	quest.2CF7B071D0F2377D.quest_desc: ["If you go on a caving adventure, you might notice rocks with yellow spots. These are sulfur ores that drop sulfur chunks. While they will be useful in some chemical processes, for now they will be used for crafting gunpowder."]
	quest.2CF7B071D0F2377D.quest_subtitle: "Don't forget to crush it"
	quest.2CF7B071D0F2377D.title: "Sulfur"
	quest.2D22795E56B387FB.quest_desc: [
		"Now you know how to make andesite alloy, you can proceed with playing with Create; the first technological part of your progression."
		""
		"First thing you need to learn about Create is that unlike other mods, Create uses its own rotational power system called Stress Capacity which is measured in &lStress Units (su)&r."
		""
		"The generator blocks such as watermills, windmills and various engines increase the Stress Capacity, then this Stress Capacity can be used in various applications."
	]
	quest.2D22795E56B387FB.title: "Create"
	quest.2DAA8042F0D25EF5.quest_desc: ["You notice that anthralite is a dense and strong material. Because of this reason, tools made of anthralite might be durable but heavy. Moreover, it seems you can make tools sharper than iron."]
	quest.2DAA8042F0D25EF5.quest_subtitle: "Heavy but durable"
	quest.2DAA8042F0D25EF5.title: "Anthralite Tools"
	quest.2E5EF7F0B82933BB.quest_desc: ["Now that you have your axe crafted, you can start harvesting wood. One thing you will notice is that you can no longer process planks from logs directly in the crafting grid. Now you need to first craft a chopping block. Just combine the same wood type on top in the crafting grid, and you will craft your first chopping block. Then just get some logs in your off hand, equip your axe in your main hand, and start processing logs into planks."]
	quest.2E5EF7F0B82933BB.quest_subtitle: "Put the logs on a chopping log"
	quest.2E5EF7F0B82933BB.title: "Chopping Logs"
	quest.2E6DC0B6597B6D40.quest_desc: ["In the ocean, you can spot some geothermal vents that are emitting smoke. Around those vents, niter dust form layers, and you can collect these. Later on, you can craft vent collectors to put on top of these vents to automate niter collection."]
	quest.2E6DC0B6597B6D40.quest_subtitle: "Cheap fertilizer"
	quest.2E6DC0B6597B6D40.title: "Niter Dust"
	quest.2F540CCDC0F1E7FF.quest_desc: ["Brass Funnels are an upgraded version of Andesite Funnels. They support filters and can transport up to a full stack of items."]
	quest.2FE48DD7D68243D2.quest_desc: ["Apart from ammunition, gunpowder can be used to craft explosives that you can throw around to make mining both fun and effective. They are cheap to craft, so consider having them with you. This way, you can extract some ores you can't normally mine with a copper pickaxe."]
	quest.2FE48DD7D68243D2.quest_subtitle: "Explosive sticks"
	quest.2FE48DD7D68243D2.title: "Dynamite"
	quest.303EEAE33B6214ED.quest_desc: ["You might be getting a little tired of crushing all the ore you've collected by hand. Build a pair of Crushing Wheels and let them crush ores and other things for you."]
	quest.303EEAE33B6214ED.quest_subtitle: "Crushing business"
	quest.30A5DD2FEAC6EB43.quest_desc: ["In a tool, the metal head part might be considered the most important part. However, handles also provide various bonuses to the final tool. For instance, using just two leather strips and a wood handle, you can craft a refined wood handle, which provides extra durability and mining speed to your tool. In the future, you'll be able to craft even more complex handles."]
	quest.30A5DD2FEAC6EB43.quest_subtitle: "Wrap your wood"
	quest.30A5DD2FEAC6EB43.title: "Refining the Tools"
	quest.31593A47330F52D0.quest_desc: ["The Black Steel Targe is a stronger version of the shield. It’s smaller than a regular shield, so it blocks less of your view during combat. It also has more durability."]
	quest.319AE20711841481.quest_desc: ["You will need a Mechanical Mixer to create brass and, later on, some special metal blends. It is also useful if you want to automate shapeless crafting recipes and some of the cooking recipes."]
	quest.31F5D662C599A925.quest_desc: [
		"Now that you have access to hardened planks, build some mills to boost your total stress capacity."
		""
		"Keep in mind that the stress consumption of Create machines has been greatly increased, and water wheels might not be enough in the long run, so you should look for stronger sources of stress production."
	]
	quest.31F5D662C599A925.quest_subtitle: "Renewable energy"
	quest.31F7B60E13C31103.quest_desc: [
		"If you don't want to find a village, or you've already found an amazing spot to build your base, you can simply spend an emerald to get your first villager."
		""
		"Just click on the icon to submit your emerald and grab your reward."
	]
	quest.31F7B60E13C31103.title: "Villager I"
	quest.34056472799EB3EE.quest_desc: ["Use a cursium ingots and the Labor Trophy to make the Iron Blueprint. With this blueprint, you’ll be able to craft iron tier guns. Also keep in mind that iron tier guns let you craft turrets, so check JEI for the different turret recipes."]
	quest.341375F9DF7CBCC0.quest_desc: ["Find a fortress in Nether, they can be easily spotted by your map. Farm a some blazes there for yourself. These will be useful for you through the pack."]
	quest.341375F9DF7CBCC0.quest_subtitle: "Even shinier sticks"
	quest.3576C2D36C252F96.quest_desc: [
		"Now, let's say you don't want to use your creosote to make hot air in the Blast Stove. In that case, place another Blast Furnace Hatch at the top middle of the Blast Furnace (one block above the opening). Then place a pump facing away from the hatch and power it. This way, you can collect a fluid called furnace gas, which can then be moved to a Blast Stove and used in place of creosote. "
		""
		"Ideally, use a different Blast Stove than your first one, since leftover creosote may block the furnace gas from entering."
		""
		"Keep in mind that the Blast Furnace produces more furnace gas than it consumes hot air, so you might also want to place a tank to store the extra gas or burn the excess using a block called \"flarestack\"."
	]
	quest.3576C2D36C252F96.title: "Furnace Gas"
	quest.35B9C5F7C9536F8A.quest_desc: [
		"The huge diesel engine is the most powerful engine you can build, and it works differently from the other two. Instead of connecting directly, it drives a shaft from a distance. Place a shaft two blocks in front of the engine and leave the block in between free, because that is where the piston moves. Once fueled, the shaft turns into an engine shaft and starts spinning."
		""
		"Huge engines do not stack like modular ones. Instead, you can point several of them at the same shaft. Their stress capacity adds up, and the shaft spins at the speed of the fastest engine. Every engine has its own small fuel tank, filled from its sides, so each one needs its own fuel line."
	]
	quest.35DD50D40E3B0367.quest_desc: [
		"Unlike stats, raising skills is as easy as pressing a button. In your Perk Up panel, you can spend XP to increase your skills. The XP cost goes up by one every time you raise that specific skill."
		""
		"You can spend the XP you earn from quests on these skill points to make your character stronger."
	]
	quest.35DD50D40E3B0367.quest_subtitle: "and where all of my xp go"
	quest.35DD50D40E3B0367.title: "Your skills"
	quest.362AA95DE254CD9C.quest_desc: [
		"Now that you have all the tools, it’s time to collect crude oil. Don’t forget that you need to run a vertical pipeline from under the Pumpjack Hole block straight down to bedrock. After that, you just need to pump the collected oil into your tanks."
		""
		"Unprocessed crude oil isn’t much use on its own, so collect it in a tank that will feed your refineries later on."
	]
	quest.362AA95DE254CD9C.quest_subtitle: "I drink your milkshake!"
	quest.362AA95DE254CD9C.title: "Crude Oil"
	quest.370A98F1283F280A.quest_desc: ["Silver armor grants good armor value, and it also has a unique effect, giving you 15 percent magic damage protection per piece. So what's the catch, you ask? Well, it has low durability, and it's also expensive to craft."]
	quest.370A98F1283F280A.quest_subtitle: "Magic protection"
	quest.370A98F1283F280A.title: "Silver Armor"
	quest.378BB47EE0192EF0.quest_desc: ["While you can turn almost any ingot into rods, only a few of them are useful so far. Electrum rods are one of those. You can make unique tool handles from them."]
	quest.378BB47EE0192EF0.quest_subtitle: "Shiny sticks"
	quest.3797A2DAAC337E67.quest_desc: ["Grab any wood log with your off hand and use your knife to carve a wooden bucket. Please note that the wooden bucket is only able to carry water and tannin water."]
	quest.3797A2DAAC337E67.quest_subtitle: "Simple bucket to carry some liquids"
	quest.3797A2DAAC337E67.title: "Wooden Bucket"
	quest.38D2CB3C9E78301F.quest_desc: ["You can get hide from various animals. The hide can't be used the same as leather; you need to process it first."]
	quest.38D2CB3C9E78301F.quest_subtitle: "No more magic leather"
	quest.38D2CB3C9E78301F.title: "Hides"
	quest.3956425EE346D389.quest_desc: [
		"Imagine you decide to set up an iron production line. After crushing cobblestone and washing it, you will end up with two products: iron and flint. You will use the iron, but the flint will most likely fill up your storage over time."
		""
		"You can place a Threshold Switch next to the chest storing the flint. When the chest becomes full, it can send a redstone signal to a chute below, allowing you to dump the excess flint automatically."
	]
	quest.3A3708DA4F4F80EA.quest_desc: ["You’ve probably noticed a trend: the bosses keep getting harder. You’ll need better guns than the copper ones. To get access to iron tier guns, we need to get the Trophy of Labor. Getting it works much like what you did for the Rusty Medal. You can either start a raid using an Iron Flare and kill the mini boss, or pay the Gunsmith a huge sum of emeralds for the trophy. It’s all up to you."]
	quest.3A3708DA4F4F80EA.quest_subtitle: "Fight or trade vol II"
	quest.3A3708DA4F4F80EA.title: "Iron Flare"
	quest.3ACE0F79E96A8DB5.quest_desc: ["Tools with an electrum handle let you break blocks more efficiently and use them faster. However, the handle greatly reduces the tool's overall durability. Perhaps, pairing it with a durable tool head might work out better."]
	quest.3ACE0F79E96A8DB5.quest_subtitle: "Faster, but what is the cost?"
	quest.3B03DCA456726664.quest_desc: [""]
	quest.3B03DCA456726664.title: "Rifles"
	quest.3B9FA833B0FAE6EB.quest_desc: ["Combine quartz with redstone dust to make rose quartz, then start polishing it. There is a special machine that lets you automate the whole polishing process, so take a look at it in JEI."]
	quest.3BC89E644DEA5E3E.quest_desc: [
		"Now that you have niter and sulfur, you can combine them with charcoal and flint to create gunpowder on the crafting table."
		""
		"Gunpowder is important for creating ammunition, so always try to have some available. Please note that later on, once you've unlocked mixers, you can increase the yield of gunpowder."
	]
	quest.3BC89E644DEA5E3E.quest_subtitle: "Building blocks of your gun-dustry"
	quest.3CA2F5FE91131B9A.quest_desc: ["Pump the nickel sludge into a Foundry Basin with a Foundry Lid and a Foundry Mixer. Feed the basin coal coke, and heat it with a superheated Blaze Burner. This turns the sludge into molten nickel. You can then cast the molten nickel into ingots using a Casting Table with an Ingot Mold on it, just like casting steel."]
	quest.3CD69EBA4D06B7A3.quest_desc: ["Mechanical Drills can be attached to contraptions to break blocks. If the contraption has any storage, the broken blocks will be transferred into it. However, their main use here is as an ingredient for the Mechanical Extruder."]
	quest.3D2AA411D0427104.quest_desc: ["Fireclay is needed to craft the blocks for the blast furnace. You can either find fireclay in the Nether or craft it yourself by combining blaze powder, refractory clay and cinder flour."]
	quest.3D2AA411D0427104.title: "Fireclay"
	quest.3D480F9E8723E025.quest_desc: ["Find a village and place the gun bench to get a gunsmith. Now you have two options: you can either spend a hefty amount of emeralds to get a rusty medal from a gunsmith villager, or you can choose violence and spend a few emeralds to get a flare gun and a copper flare from the gunsmith. It's your choice."]
	quest.3D480F9E8723E025.quest_subtitle: "or do both"
	quest.3D480F9E8723E025.title: "Fight or Trade"
	quest.3D72891113C996AD.quest_desc: ["Steel tools are your new milestone. They have no downsides and are simply better in every way than anything you’ve used so far. At the very least, make a steel pickaxe, or go all in and upgrade all of your tools to steel."]
	quest.3D72891113C996AD.quest_subtitle: "Love the way you mine"
	quest.3D72891113C996AD.title: "Steel Tools"
	quest.3D99F87FD67C959F.quest_desc: ["Funnels are crucial for item transportation and have tons of uses. Primarily, they are used to extract items from or insert items into an inventory, and their behavior can be adjusted with a wrench. Check the 'Ponder' scenes for a better idea."]
	quest.3E35B9A834EF2813.quest_desc: ["You can scrape hides by holding the hide in your off hand and any knife in your main hand. Just press and hold right-click, and scrape it to get rid of any remaining tissue. "]
	quest.3E35B9A834EF2813.quest_subtitle: "Until you figure a machine to do it for you"
	quest.3E35B9A834EF2813.title: "Scrap the Hide"
	quest.3F92AEF45FD1EDD2.quest_desc: [
		"The Winding Machine is a unique block that lets you craft some electronic components. If you’ve checked JEI and the Ponder scenes but still have no idea how it works, let me explain."
		""
		"Let’s say you want to craft a Large Coil. In JEI, you’ll see that the recipe asks you to put a Laminated Magnetic Alloy Block into a Winding Machine with a Copper Spool set to 100 turns. First, craft a Copper Spool and place it in the Winding Machine by shift right clicking the spool slot. Be careful: if you just right click, the spool will go into the wrong slot."
		""
		"Once the spool is in place and turning, you’ll notice a number pop up under it. Right click that number and change it to 10 (it’s a percentage, so 10 means 100 turns). Now place the Laminated Magnetic Alloy Block in the input slot and wait until the machine turns it into a Large Coil. Keep in mind that resistors use a Constantan Spool, not a copper one, so make sure you swap the spool before crafting resistors."
	]
	quest.406FA7E517468A24.quest_desc: ["Coal coke can be used as fuel, but that would be a bit of a waste. It is mainly used for steel production in blast furnaces. However, it cannot be used as it is. It first needs to be crushed into coke dust with a crushing wheels."]
	quest.406FA7E517468A24.quest_subtitle: "Crush the coke"
	quest.419ED50D7E771280.quest_desc: [
		"We now have all the advanced components needed to build an Arc Furnace. It’s a heavy industrial vessel that uses high-voltage electric arcs to melt and refine materials."
		""
		"Build a 3x3x2 multiblock out of fireproof blocks, then place 3 Electrode Holders on top of it. Next, put Graphite Electrodes into those holders. Now you need to supply high-voltage electricity to all 3 holders. You can do this either by building a Large Generator (see the Large Generator quest) or by running 4 generators at full speed through a 6-step Large Transformer (see the quest on setting up a Large Transformer). The Arc Furnace doesn’t need any Blaze Burners underneath."
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Now you can make steel much faster than with the Blast Furnace, and you’ll have access to new recipes to progress in the pack. Congratulations!"
	]
	quest.419ED50D7E771280.title: "Arc Furnace"
	quest.41F2DDF3B67FEF4E.quest_desc: ["If you haven't got a bronze pick yet, remember that you can use explosives to get zinc from ores. Once you finally get the zinc, you can smelt it into ingots and then turn those into nuggets. Then, you can combine these nuggets with andesite in your utility smelter to craft andesite alloy. It's a cheap, durable material that you'll be using for a few things to progress in the game."]
	quest.41F2DDF3B67FEF4E.quest_subtitle: "And your second alloy"
	quest.41F2DDF3B67FEF4E.title: "Zinc"
	quest.4404B68E1B57A632.quest_desc: ["Now that you have one, a second villager might come in handy. You can make more villagers out of them that way as well. This one is a bit more expensive than the first."]
	quest.4404B68E1B57A632.title: "Villager II"
	quest.45D1CCB753F988E0.quest_desc: ["The utility smelter is where casting really gets going. Load it with a mold and the right metal, and it forms a cast tool head ready for assembly. It also doubles as a basic alloying station, letting you combine metals into simple early game alloys like bronze and andesite alloy."]
	quest.45D1CCB753F988E0.quest_subtitle: "Two slot smelter"
	quest.4666E80C16BB690A.quest_desc: [
		"Enchanting has been completely overhauled, and the rules are simple now."
		""
		"First, you can craft any enchanted book using regular materials. Check JEI to find the recipe for any book you need. If you need an enchantment of a higher level, just combine two copies of the same book in an anvil."
		""
		"When you want to apply a book to an item, simply use an anvil. The enchanting cost never increases, and it only costs 3 levels."
	]
	quest.4666E80C16BB690A.quest_subtitle: "and how to raise them properly"
	quest.4666E80C16BB690A.title: "Enchanting overhaul"
	quest.46A4265EC3EF45A3.quest_desc: [
		"Some special multiblocks, such as the Arc Furnace, need high voltage to work, on top of their power cost, because they require a lot of current. You can build lots of generators, but since they max out at 255 V, you’ll need some kind of transformer."
		""
		"Alternatively, you can reach this high voltage by building a Large Generator. It’s a multiblock with a Rotor in the center, surrounded by 8 Stator blocks. Once you’ve placed all the blocks, start spinning the Rotor. The faster it spins, the more power, voltage and current you’ll get. Once the Rotor reaches 164 RPM, it can fully power one TFMG Arc Furnace. Be careful not to connect this generator to your other networks, since their voltages are completely different."
	]
	quest.4725257148491EDB.quest_desc: ["While you are killing some of the unusual mobs, you might notice they drop a material called ancient brass. While it has some other uses, you can use it to make yourself a handy armor set for now. This armor won't protect you that much, but it is one of the best options early on. Keep in mind that you can upgrade this armor to something stronger later on. "]
	quest.4725257148491EDB.quest_subtitle: "Let the cogs turn"
	quest.4725257148491EDB.title: "Way of the Cog Knight"
	quest.478848E7A2966C1F.quest_desc: [
		"Perks are special modifiers that you can add to your character. You can unlock them by spending experience points, and after that, you can equip and unequip them as you like. Your character has a perk capacity that limits how many perks you can equip at a time. This capacity is determined by your constitution and insight."
		""
		"Some perks add special active abilities, such as \"Dash\", which can be used with the \"C\" key. You can change this key in the controls settings if you like."
		""
		"There are many useful perks, such as double jump, 3x3 mining and enemy detection. Keep in mind that some perks are affected by certain stats and skills and get stronger over time. For more information, check the tooltips of these perks."
	]
	quest.478848E7A2966C1F.quest_subtitle: "and how you sprint faster"
	quest.478848E7A2966C1F.title: "The perks"
	quest.47A347EE4896E685.quest_desc: ["When you need to whitelist or blacklist multiple items, you can use List Filters. Simply apply them to the filter slot of blocks such as Tunnels or Funnels."]
	quest.47A9EA9984DEA7AD.quest_desc: [
		"After obtaining the horn and completing all the previous steps, there is only one thing left to do: build the blast furnace."
		""
		"The blast furnace is a 3x3 multiblock structure. Check the Ponder scene to see exactly how to build it, but keep in mind that the minimum height is three blocks."
		""
		"Once it is built, you can throw the required ingredients in through the opening at the top and start pumping hot air from the blast stove into the blast furnace hatch. As long as you provide enough hot air, the process should work just fine."
		""
		"Once the process is done, you need to pump the molten steel and slag out of the blast furnace output. Since there are two different fluids, it is a good idea to use smart fluid pipes to send each one to the right tank."
	]
	quest.47A9EA9984DEA7AD.quest_subtitle: "Finally building it"
	quest.47A9EA9984DEA7AD.title: "Blast Furnace"
	quest.4882C38F26B375FD.quest_desc: [
		"Normally, magnets are easily done using polarizers, but in order to get that point you need some magnets. This creates a problem that can only be solved by a thunder storm. Construct a lighting rod and wait for the stormy weather, when you hear the storm go outside with at least half a stack of magnetic alloy ingot. "
		""
		"Now this is the import part so read here very carefully. Place the rod in the ground and in same block throw your magnetic alloy ingots together. Get away 2 blocks from the rod and keep hover your magnetic alloy ingots. Even without a thunder hit the rod, these alloys can turn into magnet. So the moment alloys turn into magnet immediately grab them from the floor, because if you let a thunder hit the rod after this point, these magnets just going to dissapear (and this is going to hurt your feelings, we don't want that)."
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Keep in mind that obtaining magnet this way is always with a loss. So try to use these magnets in a smart way and build your functioning polarizer as soon as possible."
	]
	quest.4882C38F26B375FD.quest_subtitle: "When you hear the thunder"
	quest.4980D5B8B626BBD3.quest_desc: [
		"To measure voltage and current, we need to craft a Multimeter. If you look at any part of your electrical network while holding it, you’ll see values like voltage, current, resistance and power. If you crouch, you’ll also see the network’s total power production and consumption."
		""
		"Unfortunately, I have to break the immersion here and let you know that TFMG’s electricity is in a very buggy state right now. The developers will probably fix these bugs at some point, but I’m not sure when. For now, when you use the Multimeter, just focus on the “network power” production and consumption values."
	]
	quest.49D5E4BFA480E976.quest_desc: ["Armor crafting is a bit different now. Your choices are limited in the beginning if you want better armor values than the leather set. If you've unlocked bronze picks, it means you can mine some silver to make a silver set; if not, a copper set might work for you. Check the next entries in the quest line to see what each armor offers."]
	quest.49D5E4BFA480E976.quest_subtitle: "Choices"
	quest.49D5E4BFA480E976.title: "Armor "
	quest.49FA4C145DFEC442.quest_desc: [
		"Take your tool handle and the pickaxe head you cast in a crafting table and just put them together to assemble your first tool. Quick reminder in case you missed it: sticks are not handles, make sure you've transformed them into a wood handle with a knife, or better, upgrade it into a refined wood handle to get extra stats on your final tool."
		""
		"Once you assemble your tool, you won't be able to break it back into parts, and if it runs out of durability, it will just disappear forever. Luckily for you, there are ways to repair your tools, which will be revealed later on."
	]
	quest.49FA4C145DFEC442.quest_subtitle: "Assemble the parts"
	quest.49FA4C145DFEC442.title: "Your First Tool"
	quest.4A900B36063E8371.quest_desc: [
		"Sulfuric acid will be the first thing we produce in the mixer. We’ll need it to process nickel ore and to make etched circuit boards."
		""
		"Put sulfur dust and nitrate dust into the mixer multiblock along with water, and it will produce sulfuric acid. Pump it into a tank for later use."
	]
	quest.4A900B36063E8371.title: "Sulfuric Acid"
	quest.4C62404549BC1C60.quest_desc: [
		"Your first multiblock will be the mixer. Even though the Ponder scenes show it as 3x3x2, you can get away with a 2x2x1 size, and it will work just fine. After you build the multiblock, place your Industrial Mixer block on top and attach the Mixer Blade to it. Don’t forget to connect the Industrial Mixer to your stress network with a shaft."
		""
		"Some recipes require heat, so place one or two Blaze Burners under the multiblock."
	]
	quest.4C62404549BC1C60.title: "Mixer Multiblock"
	quest.4CBFF5E478ABEDBA.quest_desc: ["Want to build a car in Minecraft, but don’t want to use crushing wheels? Well, then craft some tires with the rubber you just made."]
	quest.4D4486E9161001CB.title: "Deployer"
	quest.4DD14B4D42ED4013.quest_desc: ["Some of the early Create machines require crude mechanisms to craft, so it's worth making a few extra now. You'll also need them later as the base material for crafting precision mechanisms."]
	quest.4DD14B4D42ED4013.quest_subtitle: "Easy to make"
	quest.4DFDE2C81F6681C4.quest_desc: ["These three ammo types will be the ones you use for now. Grab the casings and tips you produce and start making some rounds following the assembly sequence. If you can, try to make production lines to automate your ammo production."]
	quest.4DFDE2C81F6681C4.quest_subtitle: "All the ammo you need"
	quest.4DFDE2C81F6681C4.title: "Ammo - Copper"
	quest.4E0F0CAD22CA635B.quest_desc: ["Now that you have magnets and Steel Mechanisms, you can build a Generator. This block turns stress units into electricity. Keep in mind that this kind of energy is different from Forge Energy (FE) or Redstone Flux (RF). The system has some complexity to it, but for now, all you need to know is that the faster the generator spins, the more power it generates."]
	quest.4E49FDE5AC94B798.quest_desc: [
		"Diesel engines are loud, and a room full of them quickly becomes unbearable. The engine silencer fixes that: attach it to any diesel engine and it becomes almost completely quiet."
		""
		"The turbocharger forces extra air into the engine, letting it burn its fuel far more effectively. Attach it to a diesel engine or a modular diesel engine to double both its speed and its stress capacity."
		""
		"An engine can only hold one upgrade, so you will have to choose between power and silence."
	]
	quest.500585976CB35B6F.quest_desc: [
		"Depots serve as stationary inventories for processing items. For instance, if you don't want to use a full production line for making plates, simply place a Depot under the Mechanical Press. You can deposit and retrieve items by right clicking the Depot."
		""
		"There are tons of other uses, so don't forget to check the 'Ponder' scene for this block"
	]
	quest.515872E7F6BCB3D1.quest_desc: [
		"With so many hardships behind you, you'll finally be able to craft a gun bench for yourself (or stole one from a village). Well, congratulations! Now, also craft your first blueprint as well. "
		""
		"These blueprints are used to craft guns, and the antique blueprint is the first tier you can craft. There isn't much you can craft with it so far, but take these rewards to proceed to your next quest."
	]
	quest.515872E7F6BCB3D1.quest_subtitle: "Look at these cool parts"
	quest.515872E7F6BCB3D1.title: "Guns, Guns, Guns"
	quest.516BE923B7A0FCB7.quest_desc: [
		"To build a Blast Furnace, you need the horn of the Netherite Monstrosity. But first, you need to find out where it is. Craft a Monstrous Eye and use it in the Nether to locate the boss."
		""
		"It works similarly to an Eye of Ender, but you don't need to pick the item back up. There is just a cooldown between uses."
	]
	quest.516BE923B7A0FCB7.quest_subtitle: "Track the monstrosity"
	quest.51A0B0BA61FD2710.quest_desc: ["Capacitor is a basic crafting components for electrical blocks, but most importantly, it's needed to craft circuit boards."]
	quest.51BC278067F60E8B.quest_desc: ["There are two types of connections for extending your electrical network: cables and hubs. Cables run in one direction and connect one point to another. Hubs, on the other hand, can connect on all sides. Also, if a hub is connected to a block that accepts FE, it will automatically convert electricity into FE."]
	quest.51E4C0C0CE385D05.quest_desc: [
		"Cauldrons can now be crafted using lead ingots instead. Metal cauldrons have one additional use when it comes to leather processing."
		""
		"Moreover, you can use these cauldrons to collect resin from pine trees or syrup from maple trees by combining them with a tree tap. Just find the tree, put a tap on it, then place a cauldron under the tap and wait until it collects some tree sap."
	]
	quest.51E4C0C0CE385D05.quest_subtitle: "Tap on a tree"
	quest.51E4C0C0CE385D05.title: "Cauldron"
	quest.529658EE046CD1E4.quest_desc: ["You can dispose of extra organic material in advanced composters to obtain bonemeal, niter and phosphor dust for yourself. You can build them in masses to create a good supply of gunpowder material."]
	quest.529658EE046CD1E4.quest_subtitle: "Compost your food scraps"
	quest.529658EE046CD1E4.title: "Advanced Composting"
	quest.53399020FFFB825F.quest_desc: ["Now that you've scraped the hide, we still need to clean it. You can either drop the hide into a water source or wash it in a wooden cauldron filled with water. Later on you can use fans to wash the hide clean."]
	quest.53399020FFFB825F.quest_subtitle: "Just drop them into the river"
	quest.53399020FFFB825F.title: "Clean the Hide"
	quest.5604487B71991805.quest_desc: ["When treated iron blend is fed into a Bloomery, it turns into treated iron ingots. This ingot can be used as an alternative to iron in some recipes, as well as in recipes for guns."]
	quest.5612FA51A844800E.quest_desc: ["To progress further, we need to find out how to make black steel and cursium. To start our journey, we need to find the Frosted Prison, a huge castle located in snowy biomes. Just like we found the Soul Forge using the Monstrous Eye, we now need to use the Cursed Eye. Craft the eye and start your search. Good luck!"]
	quest.5612FA51A844800E.quest_subtitle: "Frosted prison"
	quest.56BFBE54585CC057.quest_desc: [
		"Every machine with a cog needs stress units to run. As your factory grows, you’ll need more and more stress. Sadly, renewable energy is all a lie. Of course, you could daisy chain hundreds of water wheels to get the stress you need. But what if I told you there’s a better alternative?"
		""
		"Craft these oil extraction tools. Check out their Ponder scenes too, and get familiar with how they work."
	]
	quest.56BFBE54585CC057.quest_subtitle: "There will be blood"
	quest.575F8424035E65F2.quest_desc: [
		"Now you have a steady supply of copper rounds. You have more refined options when it comes to your arsenal. No more shooting pebbles!"
		""
		"Some important boss fights are coming, so my suggestion would be to craft at least two types of guns with you."
	]
	quest.575F8424035E65F2.quest_subtitle: "Better guns"
	quest.575F8424035E65F2.title: "New blueprint"
	quest.583F30DF573873BA.quest_desc: ["Chutes act as item pipes or hoppers that only allow items to travel downward. If you want them to move items upward, you need to place fans underneath them."]
	quest.58C66BA27ECB815B.quest_desc: ["If you have never used potions before, now it is time. Make a brewing stand and start brewing. Check JEI for potion effects. There are some extra added ones you might find really useful. "]
	quest.58C66BA27ECB815B.quest_subtitle: "Brewing is so underrated"
	quest.59865728794ADA5D.quest_desc: ["Precision Mechanisms are mainly used to craft advanced logistics blocks from Create. Later on, they will also be used as an ingredient in more complex parts. If you ever find yourself with plenty of stress capacity, try to set up a production line for them."]
	quest.5A7E1B010C571D00.quest_desc: [
		"Now that we have the Electrolyzer multiblock and bauxite dust, we can make aluminum. Make sure both electrodes are getting enough electricity (you can check this with the Multimeter) and are working."
		""
		"Heat the Blaze Burners under the multiblock to heat level 2. Then feed bauxite dust into the Electrolyzer through a chute. It will turn into aluminum ingots and nuggets. Extract them with a filtered funnel; otherwise, the bauxite will be extracted too."
		""
		"Be careful: this process creates carbon dioxide as a byproduct. Simply pump the carbon dioxide out and dispose of it in a smokestack or an exhaust."
	]
	quest.5C23303C9A10EC8C.quest_desc: ["If you haven’t gotten rid of your Anthralite set yet, it might be a good idea to craft it into Adrien Armor. It offers good protection as well as armor toughness. Only downside is that demands precious steel."]
	quest.5C23303C9A10EC8C.title: "Adrien Armor"
	quest.5CB6D03615607199.quest_desc: ["Forging allows you craft superior tools. &4To do that, just grab a metal block in your off hand, then start right clicking until it turns into a pickaxe head. If you need another type of head, just put the head you smithed back into your off hand and keep right clicking again until you find the tool head you need.&r"]
	quest.5CB6D03615607199.quest_subtitle: "Smash the block"
	quest.5CB6D03615607199.title: "Your First Forged Tool"
	quest.5D332B07D914F103.quest_desc: ["By combining flint with a stick, you can craft your first knife. For now, you can use your knife to cut grass; this action sometimes gets you straw that you can use in various recipes. Later on, we will use knives in other areas."]
	quest.5D332B07D914F103.quest_subtitle: "Your first utility tool"
	quest.5E0AE40FEEC68BA5.quest_desc: ["Hides aren't the only thing you can scrape. &4Hold a stick in your off hand and start scraping it with your flint knife to get your first Wood Handle.&r This handle lets you build far more capable tools than your crude flint ones. Just combine the Wood Handle with a casted or forged tool head, and you'll have yourself a proper tool."]
	quest.5E0AE40FEEC68BA5.quest_subtitle: "STICKS ≠ WOOD HANDLE"
	quest.5E0AE40FEEC68BA5.title: "Wood Handle"
	quest.5E4644FDF829ED82.quest_desc: ["Use the black steel ingots you got from the prison to craft the Sturdy Whisk, and then the Foundry Mixer. This block makes alloys much faster than the Utility Smelter. For now, it’s also your only way to produce nickel."]
	quest.5E4644FDF829ED82.title: "Foundry Mixer"
	quest.5EDAA89684D15459.quest_desc: [
		"Effects are passive buffs that your character gains. Simply put, certain combinations of stats and skills create these effects. For instance, when you increase your agility stat and your athletics skill, you will notice that you sprint faster."
		""
		"Effects scale with the balance between a stat and a skill, not just their sum. If one is high and the other is low, the effect barely grows, raising only the stat, or only the skill, won't get you far. To make real progress, you need to raise both roughly together."
		""
		"If you want to know the exact calculation, here is how it works:"
		""
		"Take the geometric mean of the stat and the skill, then divide it by 10. The square root of this value determines the level of your effect."
	]
	quest.5EDAA89684D15459.quest_subtitle: "and how you sprint faster"
	quest.5EDAA89684D15459.title: "The effects"
	quest.5F65A46904A94337.quest_desc: [
		"Whether you paid the hefty price or actually killed the raid boss, you got the medal, congratulations! You can proceed with your progression now."
		""
		"Don't forget to take this generator as a reward. It simply generates stress capacity by burning fuel. You will need it until you figure out a way to create stress capacity by your own way."
	]
	quest.5F65A46904A94337.quest_subtitle: "Your first trophy"
	quest.5F65A46904A94337.title: "Rusty Medal"
	quest.5FD282AFAE383172.quest_desc: ["Mix nickel with limesand and sulfuric acid in the mixer multiblock to create nickel sludge. Then pump the sludge into a Foundry Basin."]
	quest.5FD282AFAE383172.title: "Nickel Sludge"
	quest.606EF5C853EDB677.quest_desc: ["You can place Chain Drives side by side to relay rotational force sideways. The RPM of each Chain Drive will be the same."]
	quest.60915EB511E37D95.quest_desc: ["Remember when you almost drowned trying to collect those niter dust layers from the ocean floor? Just put one of these bad boys on top of the vent and enjoy your auto collected niter dust. If you are living away from the vent make sure to load the chunk while you are gone."]
	quest.60915EB511E37D95.title: "Niter Collection"
	quest.61039AD108A3D9ED.title: "Sniper Rifles"
	quest.612CEF6F41EBC4A5.quest_desc: [
		"If you crush basalt, you might get some vanadium nuggets. You can then use them to make black steel."
		""
		"Basalt can be found in large amounts in the Nether’s Basalt Deltas biome."
	]
	quest.629AB4474CA61A27.quest_desc: ["Cutting boards are interactive blocks that let you put various items on them and cut them with different tools. There are many recipes; you can take a look by pressing \"U\" while hovering over a cutting board in your inventory."]
	quest.629AB4474CA61A27.quest_subtitle: "on a cutting board"
	quest.629AB4474CA61A27.title: "Cut the Wood"
	quest.63871FB5666F1613.quest_desc: ["Now that you have access to cast iron, you can make a pot and a stove. These unlock many advanced cooking recipes. Check the Perk Up chapter to learn more about cooking."]
	quest.63871FB5666F1613.quest_subtitle: "Eating outside is expensive, time to cook"
	quest.63871FB5666F1613.title: "Pot on a Stove"
	quest.644FE6A7D4E19405.quest_desc: ["In order to produce leather, you need to make some tannin water, and to get tannin water, we need to find tree bark. You can place logs on cutting boards and cut them with axes to get their bark. Tree bark has a few more uses, so you might consider debarking the logs first, before you process them in a chopping block to get planks."]
	quest.644FE6A7D4E19405.quest_subtitle: "Always debark your log first"
	quest.644FE6A7D4E19405.title: "Tree Barks"
	quest.647DD1BB54826F04.quest_desc: ["The redstone link is used to send and receive redstone signals. By sneak right clicking with a wrench on a redstone link, its signal can be changed between sending and receiving. The frequency can be also customized by assignin and item or block to frequency slots, when these slots share the same frequency slots they linked with each other. "]
	quest.64E5DAC31FB3470B.quest_desc: [
		"If you haven't found any coal yet, just get the charcoal from the previous quest reward and craft a campfire. Make yourself cozy!"
		""
		"Campfires are also essential now. They will give you access to some important recipes and provide you with a place to respawn. Oh, and for your information, there's no sleeping in this pack, &2just right-click on a campfire while crouching to set your spawn point.&r"
		""
		"Also, you'll notice that the campfire is unlit. To light it, you can craft a simple fire starter with just two sticks and start blasting it on the campfire."
	]
	quest.64E5DAC31FB3470B.quest_subtitle: "What do you mean there is no sleep?"
	quest.64E5DAC31FB3470B.title: "How to Make a Fire with Two Sticks"
	quest.6569A43BE07E08C3.quest_desc: [
		"You might notice that all the ores you gather are literally vanishing before your eyes to feed your obsession with making the factory bigger. Well, now that you have access to steel, you might want to process your ores further into dusts."
		""
		"With the Helve Hammer, you can increase your ore yield by pulverizing your crushed ores. This way, you can double your yield once more after crushing them. The only downside is that the Helve Hammer is a bit slow and needs quite a lot of stress capacity to run at higher speeds."
		""
		"I highly recommend adding it to your ore processing line."
	]
	quest.6569A43BE07E08C3.quest_subtitle: "Crushing business vol II"
	quest.65EEB157DBFE477C.quest_desc: ["Steam engines are a primitive yet effective way to generate stress units when you build a lot of them together. Build a large Fluid Tank, place Blaze Burners under it, and attach the engines to the tank. Once you pump water into the tank, it will start generating steam. However, you might find that steam engines aren’t as strong as you remember."]
	quest.662CBECD7DFCA048.title: "Feasts"
	quest.67AC5F7470EDEABB.quest_desc: [
		"The hammer is expensive, but totally worth it. Now, instead of casting metals into tool parts, you can just turn blocks into tool head parts. This way you can create superior tools that have better durability and efficiency compared to their cast versions."
		""
		"Now, this isn't the only use for the hammer. You can also smash any ore into crushed ore, doubling your yield. The downside is it takes manual time, so perhaps this is only worth it with precious ores."
		""
		"The last thing you can do with the hammer is crafting plates from ingots. Those will be important later on as well."
	]
	quest.67AC5F7470EDEABB.quest_subtitle: "Smash everything"
	quest.686B1033D9F3B247.quest_desc: ["Transistor is a basic crafting components for electrical blocks, but most importantly, it's needed to craft circuit boards."]
	quest.688FFBD65D75AA86.quest_desc: [
		"There are some dangers out there that might cause you to die by suffocation or poisonous gas. In this situation, it is always good to have a respirator at the ready. "
		""
		"Also, consider creating some gas grenades. They're really effective at mass killing mobs, and you won't be affected by them as long as you wear a respirator."
	]
	quest.693EC5716DE95FAC.quest_desc: [
		"Perk Up is a mod that allows you to progress your character in a deeper manner. Eating food now improves your stats, and spending XP increases your skill points. Increasing stats and skills grants your character various bonuses. You can also purchase various perks to grant yourself unique abilities."
		""
		"You can check your character panel by pressing the \"B\" button. "
	]
	quest.693EC5716DE95FAC.title: "Perk Up"
	quest.699B6835D824D4C7.quest_desc: ["You realized that blaze rods can be used as handles when combined with warped stems. Tools made with these handles deal more damage. However, you also noticed that blaze handles make the tool significantly more brittle."]
	quest.699B6835D824D4C7.quest_subtitle: "Magic handle"
	quest.699B6835D824D4C7.title: "Blaze Handle"
	quest.69A82B19C7FA9CCD.quest_desc: ["Now that you have access to more refined materials and mechanical crafters, you can make better armor for yourself. Try making a set of treated brass armor. It lacks armor toughness, but it definitely provides good protection and comes with knockback resistance as a bonus."]
	quest.69A82B19C7FA9CCD.title: "Treated Brass Armor"
	quest.69E7C2A45B54F180.quest_desc: [
		"You have your molten steel in the tank, but you are probably wondering how that fluid is going to turn into ingots. Well, this is where the casting table, the casting basin and all the molds come into play."
		""
		"Craft some graphite by combining clay with any type of coal. Then press it with a mechanical press into a blank graphite mold. Next, shape it with a stonecutter to make an ingot mold. Place this mold on top of the casting table and pump the molten steel into the table. Let the ingot cool down, then right click the table to get your very first ingot."
		""
		"You can also use a casting basin to make metal blocks from molten metal if you want. Just pump the molten metal into the basin instead."
	]
	quest.69E7C2A45B54F180.quest_subtitle: "One final step"
	quest.69FA1B67654C75A6.quest_desc: ["Leather doesn't provide not much of a protection but still it is essential for you to stay alive for now. Also future armor you will craft will allways start with leather armor. "]
	quest.69FA1B67654C75A6.quest_subtitle: "It is something"
	quest.69FA1B67654C75A6.title: "Leather Armor"
	quest.6C0BF80C98ABAD62.quest_desc: ["Circuit boards are made in 4 steps. First, craft the board using plastic and green dye. Then, place a Golden Sheet on the board. Next, put these coated boards into the mixer multiblock with sulfuric acid to make etched circuit boards. Finally, add resistors, transistors and capacitors to the board to finish your circuit board."]
	quest.6C4905E90FE2E4ED.quest_desc: [
		"You notice that your tools getting broken fast. You might want to invest in unbreaking. "
		""
		"Or perhaps you want your tools to work faster? Then craft efficiency books."
	]
	quest.6E1B22FB525ADA7B.quest_desc: ["Perhaps you don't want to deal with all the logistics of drilling and refining, and you are okay to use an inferior fuel as long as it is renewable. If it is what you wish then craft some fermenters. "]
	quest.6E312592FCCD6E7C.quest_desc: ["Resistor is a basic crafting components for electrical blocks, but most importantly, it's needed to craft circuit boards."]
	quest.6FCA40810BD3E360.quest_desc: [
		"Creosote can be used to craft hardened planks. These planks are required for some Create machines and, later on, for making Steel Casings."
		""
		"Apart from crafting, creosote can also be used as a fuel source for blaze burners. Also, it is needed in blast stoves to keep the blast furnace running."
	]
	quest.6FCA40810BD3E360.quest_subtitle: "Precious tar"
	quest.720E6A707C89CCA9.quest_desc: [
		"Before you face the Monstrosity, make sure you have enough ammo with you. Bring good quality food, because you will need it. Using a fire resistance potion would also make this fight a lot easier."
		""
		"Also, it is a good idea to invest in agility and athletics to increase your movement speed, along with a perk called \"Dash\", which lets you dodge some of the attacks using button \"C\"."
		""
		"One final note: when fighting bosses or enemies with high armor, try not to use shotguns. A shotgun's total damage is split between its individual pellets, and against an enemy with high armor, the armor formula applies to each pellet separately. This makes the final damage much lower. Instead, try to use guns that fire single bullets with high damage."
	]
	quest.72764501A7AEE989.quest_desc: [
		"Now that you’ve found the prison, it’s time to kill some mobs. Keep in mind that this structure is really dangerous. Before you dive in and explore it, make sure you have enough ammo, medical supplies, food and gear. Also, don’t forget to set your spawn point at a campfire near the structure."
		""
		"Some of the Draugr use shields, so you either need to hit them with an axe first to break their block, or let them hit you once so you get a moment to shoot them."
		""
		"The mini bosses here are very dangerous, so blast them before they get a chance to attack you. They drop a strange key item that lets you open the boss’s chamber in the cellar."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		""
		"Once you have 5 black steel ingots, you can leave for now. That’s all we need to start processing nickel."
		""
		"If you’re feeling strong, with good stats, skills, perks and armor, plus plenty of supplies, you can try to kill the boss as well. It will drop some cursium ingots. Try to save at least one ingot for later, since you’ll need it as a catalyst to craft more cursium ingots."
	]
	quest.72764501A7AEE989.quest_subtitle: "Let's not rush this"
	quest.72C76C168AE92987.quest_desc: ["Treated iron blend is made by mixing cast iron with niter dust and lime sand in a basin and a blaze burner underneath. "]
	quest.72C76C168AE92987.quest_subtitle: "Process it again"
	quest.7389602E36F44469.quest_desc: ["Smart Chutes can be filtered and can also be disabled with a redstone signal."]
	quest.742A66D059040C76.quest_desc: [
		"Make yourself a huge shopping list, including quartz, glowstone, fireclay, nether warts, blaze rod, blaze powder, magma cream and whatever else you can find in this hellish place. "
		""
		"One suggestion I can give you is not to skip the potion brewing side of the game. It is no longer an easy game, so try to take advantage of everything."
	]
	quest.742A66D059040C76.quest_subtitle: "Hot and Spooky"
	quest.742A66D059040C76.title: "Nether"
	quest.74517FBD4422BF7E.quest_desc: [
		"Straw is a simple item crafted with a Rolling Mill. Right clicking a Blaze Burner with straw turns it into a new block: the Blaze Burner with Straw. Certain fluids can be pumped into these to make them heated or superheated. It’s basically a better alternative to hand feeding charcoal to your blazes."
		""
		"More importantly, certain fluids like LPG and biodiesel can superheat Blaze Burners, which makes them a better alternative to blaze cakes. Check the Blaze Burner recipes in JEI to see which fluids you can use."
	]
	quest.74B9EC17C2915622.quest_desc: ["The carbon dioxide byproduct currently has no use, so it needs to be disposed of. You can do this by pumping it into an Exhaust."]
	quest.7536EE9E6396317B.quest_desc: [
		"When the Mechanical Saw is powered, it can turn logs into planks more efficiently, yielding six planks instead of four. Shafts and leather strips can also be made more efficiently with it."
		""
		"Shaping molds also requires the Mechanical Saw. However, it is better to use a Stonecutter instead, since the Mechanical Saw picks a random mold shape unless you give it a filter."
	]
	quest.75DBCF1296690039.quest_desc: ["With Gearshifts, you can change the direction of rotation using a Redstone signal."]
	quest.75F856C3A5073E4C.quest_desc: ["Iron is an overall better material for tool making. Moreover, pickaxes made of iron can mine obsidian. Grab an iron block and start forging your new tool heads!"]
	quest.75F856C3A5073E4C.title: "Iron Tools"
	quest.77E6DA403D0336A9.quest_desc: ["Perhaps you remember it was mentioned that the cutting board has more uses. Well, you can use a cutting board to cut your leather into strips. Just place some leather on a cutting board and right click it with a knife."]
	quest.77E6DA403D0336A9.quest_subtitle: "Strips of leather"
	quest.77E6DA403D0336A9.title: "Leather Strip"
	quest.7883564F59F2B03D.quest_desc: ["Food is no longer as simple as stuffing yourself with baked potatoes and forgetting about it. Now, if you want to get stronger, you need to eat different kinds of food."]
	quest.7927E134DDE007B6.quest_desc: [
		"I hope you’ve finally figured out how to use the Blast Furnace effectively. You’ve probably realized you’ll need a lot of steel, so it might be a good idea to make some Blast Furnace Reinforcements. That way, you can produce steel faster."
		""
		"These blocks go in two places: on top of your fireproof blocks as a cover, and on the corners, replacing the fireproof brick reinforcements. Once your blast furnace is fully covered, look at its output block with Engineer’s Goggles and you’ll see the word “Reinforced”."
	]
	quest.7927E134DDE007B6.quest_subtitle: "We need more steel"
	quest.7927E134DDE007B6.title: "Improved Blast Furnace"
	quest.79EBA894DDDEED20.quest_desc: [
		"Heavy oil is the first main product you’ll get from refining crude oil. You can burn it as fuel in Huge Engines to generate a good amount of stress capacity, or process it further in another distillation tower to turn it into other products. You’ll also need heavy oil to make rubber."
		""
		"Check JEI to see which distillation recipe best suits your needs."
	]
	quest.79EBA894DDDEED20.title: "Heavy Oil"
	quest.7A2E95CCE3A97777.quest_desc: ["There is no sleeping in this pack, and maybe you didn't notice, but your flint tools are not going to protect you. For tonight, the best you can do is get these torches, create a large lit area, and defend yourself with this musket. Good luck! You'll need it."]
	quest.7A2E95CCE3A97777.quest_subtitle: "Prepare for the night"
	quest.7A2E95CCE3A97777.title: "Danger"
	quest.7B28681EF92ED43F.quest_desc: [
		"You don't have access to iron yet, but no worries, using andesite alloy blocks and ingots, you can craft an anvil out of them."
		""
		"The anvil will be essential to your journey. &4You can repair your items indefinitely, spending only 1 level, or add new enchants to your tools and armor by spending 3 levels.&r Don't forget these level costs are all constant, meaning they always cost you the same number of levels, so don't shy away from upgrading your gear regularly."
	]
	quest.7BB741416E898139.quest_desc: [
		"If you find yourself dying frequently, consider applying protection enchantments. These can be added to your armor using an anvil, and they will remain even after you upgrade the armor."
		""
		"Keep in mind that each armor piece can only have one type of protection enchantment, so choose wisely."
	]
	quest.7BB741416E898139.quest_subtitle: "Don't die so fast"
	quest.7BB741416E898139.title: "Protection"
	quest.7BE70F3DCE868E58.quest_desc: [
		"With the parts you get from the previous quest, you can only craft one of these guns. Choose wisely, because you won't be able to craft your own weapons until you figure out how to process iron."
		""
		"After you finish this quest, take your repair kits as a reward. You can use them to repair your guns on an anvil. Just a note: each repair kit fully repairs your weapons, so use those kits wisely as well."
	]
	quest.7BE70F3DCE868E58.quest_subtitle: "Tough decisions"
	quest.7BE70F3DCE868E58.title: "And More Guns"
	quest.7BFFABFA068B09B3.quest_desc: ["When naphtha is heated in the mixer multiblock, it turns into propylene and ethylene. If you can, build a separate mixer multiblock just for these two fluids."]
	quest.7BFFABFA068B09B3.title: "Prophylene - Ethylene"
	quest.7C3FDE922CEE9C85.quest_desc: ["The crafting table is just your usual spot for 3x3 crafting. Don't worry though, soon you'll be crafting in far more complex ways."]
	quest.7C3FDE922CEE9C85.quest_subtitle: "Same old boring crafting table"
	quest.7C3FDE922CEE9C85.title: "Crafting Table"
	quest.7C4194B33D8CF053.quest_desc: [
		"If you haven’t killed the Frosted Prison’s boss, Maledictus, yet, now is a good time to do it. Make sure you have good stats, gear and supplies for the fight. It will be hard, but it’s manageable. Just keep moving and shooting, and you’ll be fine."
		""
		"Once you get your first cursium ingot, you can duplicate it in the Arc Furnace (the recipe is shown under chemical vat in JEI) using emeralds and black steel ingots. The cursium ingots you make will be really important for your factory."
	]
	quest.7C4DDC7EAB730F56.quest_desc: ["Now that you have access to brass and Electron Tubes, you can craft Mechanical Crafters. When they are placed and powered, they can be used to craft items that require more than a 3x3 crafting grid."]
	quest.7C4DDC7EAB730F56.quest_subtitle: "3x3 crafting is lame"
	quest.7C4DDC7EAB730F56.title: "Mechanical Crafting"
	quest.7C9477BB23CE1B57.quest_desc: ["Now that we have electricity running, it’s time to put it to use: let’s build an Electrolyzer multiblock so we can process aluminum. Much like the mixer multiblock, you can build it as a 2x2x2 using Steel Chemical Vats (Cast Iron Chemical Vats won’t work). After you build the multiblock, place two Electrode Holders on it and put a copper or zinc electrode in each one."]
	quest.7CC16CB9E5E11345.quest_desc: [
		"Sugar cane is important. You can craft paper from it, which sees a lot of use in early ammunition and later in a lot of recipes."
		""
		"Also consider crafting sugar, and try some recipes that use sugar. If you slice a cake or a pie on a cutting board, you might be surprised by the stat gain coming from those slices."
	]
	quest.7CC16CB9E5E11345.quest_subtitle: "Sugarcane papers"
	quest.7CC16CB9E5E11345.title: "Sugar Cane"
	quest.7CC35D14FDA9EBFD.quest_desc: ["At this point, you are probably wondering where all the promised automation is. Well, let's start simple. Craft yourself some Mechanical Belts. Click on one Shaft, then click on a parallel Shaft, and voilà! The two are connected, and you have your first production line. Don't forget: you can use belts to connect two separate kinetic networks with each other."]
	quest.7D921CC2A17A15BD.quest_desc: ["At first with a flint pickaxe you can only collect and process copper, tin and lead ores. All of these metals have their uses. So collect them as you explore."]
	quest.7D921CC2A17A15BD.quest_subtitle: "Be proud"
	quest.7D921CC2A17A15BD.title: "Your First Metal Ingots"
	quest.7D9348152E915519.quest_desc: [
		"The Coke Oven is a wonderful device that lets you refine fuels such as coal into coke. While doing so, it also produces creosote and carbon dioxide as byproducts. You can pump the creosote out from the back and the carbon dioxide from the top. Currently, there is no use for carbon dioxide, so it should be vented through an exhaust or a smokestack."
		""
		"You can feed coal into the Coke Oven with a hopper or a chute. When the coke is ready, it is automatically ejected from the front."
		""
		"Keep in mind that this is a multiblock structure that forms automatically. It needs to be one block wide and can be either 2x2 or 3x3 (height x depth)."
	]
	quest.7D9348152E915519.quest_subtitle: "Heat the coal"
	quest.7DEA440017FCA279.quest_desc: ["When you process sulfur and heavy oil in a heated mixer multiblock, you’ll get rubber sheets. Rubber has some really important uses, like crafting tires, cables and the fireproof blocks for the Arc Furnace, but it can also be turned into synthetic leather."]
	quest.7E249006D8FB5BCB.quest_desc: [
		"Hey, thanks for playing Chapter Three. I hope you enjoyed it! Now I’d like to ask for your help. We currently have a cool variety of industrial machines that handle different processes. If you have an idea for a process you think we could add to the game, don’t be shy, get in touch with me. And if you have thoughts on any current processes that you think could be better, contact me about those too."
		""
		"From now on, instead of pushing updates every 2 weeks, I’ll just push them whenever there’s a significant change in the pack. That way, I can get rid of game breaking bugs as soon as I catch them. Speaking of bugs, if you’ve made it this far, you’ve probably run into millions of them, so I’d really appreciate it if you joined the Discord and reported them to me."
		""
		"Thank you again for taking the time to play my pack. Take care of yourself."
		""
		"See you soon,"
		"Ziggo"
		""
		"[ { \"text\": \"Discord\", \"underlined\": true, \"clickEvent\": { \"action\": \"open_url\", \"value\": \"https://discord.gg/ndS7mSRPtR\" } } ]"
	]
	quest.7E249006D8FB5BCB.title: "Check this"
	quest.7E45C027BB43B3DF.quest_desc: [
		"You must really be tired of your old, useless flint pickaxe. Let's craft you a proper one. First, put one pickaxe head mold and one block of metal of your choice (copper or bronze) into a utility smelter; this will grant you a cast tool head."
		""
		"Cast tools are inferior compared to their forged versions, but at this stage of the game, casting tool heads is all you can do."
		""
		"One final note: bronze can harvest iron tier ores, whereas copper can only harvest stone tier. So you might want to think twice before spending a copper block on a pickaxe tool head."
	]
	quest.7E45C027BB43B3DF.quest_subtitle: "Which one is brighter?"
	quest.7E45C027BB43B3DF.title: "Your First Tool Head"
	quest.7E507A84A1874C9F.quest_desc: [
		"At this point in your playthrough, you may start to run out of ores around your base. Luckily, we know we can crush certain special stones to get certain metal ores. The problem is that the chance of a stone containing that ore is so low that it isn’t practical to collect enough stone to produce even a few crushed ores."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"However, now that we have Mechanical Extruders, we can generate endless stone. The special ore-bearing stones can only be generated if a block of cursium is placed next to the Mechanical Extruder. So, place a cursium block and a block of the metal you want to produce next to a Mechanical Extruder, power it, and it will start producing the stone you need. You can then crush these stones into crushed ores with Crushing Wheels. Check the recipes in JEI to see which stone you need to generate and crush."
		""
		"&2Tip:&r You can place up to 4 Mechanical Extruders around a single cursium block if you want to save on cursium blocks."
	]
	quest.7EF9536401DB7E3A.quest_desc: ["If you're willing to spend some extra leather, you can craft a saddle. Keep in mind that horses in this modpack are smarter and can do things they normally can't."]
	quest.7EF9536401DB7E3A.quest_subtitle: "Neigh!"
	quest.7F43B5E4991CFE05.quest_desc: [
		"You've chosen violence, great! Now, this is how raids work. You put a flare in your off hand, then fire it with your flare gun to call a raid. The raid comes with a boss and a few guard mobs around it, and the boss can shoot, and shoot fast, so don't try to engage in melee in this state, you'll just get mowed down immediately. Either put yourself strategically at a point where you can hide behind blocks, or try to fight in a big open field where you can hit and run them. Either way, stock up on good food, bandages and armor, you'll need it."
		""
		"If you find yourself in a desperate situation that you think you can't kill the boss, then just spend some extra emeralds to get the rusty medal instead. You can always come back and try again after you've gotten better gear. Good luck!"
	]
	quest.7F43B5E4991CFE05.quest_subtitle: "Kill 'em all"
	quest.7F43B5E4991CFE05.title: "How to Spawn Raids"
	reward_table.52095187CF93F7A0.title: "Ore Reward II"
	reward_table.5647CCB6D1B26A28.title: "Ore Reward"
	task.1DDA6AA9D65ECF91.title: "Hide"
	task.3244C46CADAA13A7.title: "Iron tools"
	task.5472BCBB5F90B2A2.title: "Chopping Logs"
}
